140: ---
141: 
142: ## Working with Translations 🌐
143: 
144: This project follows the [official internationalization guide for Flutter][internationalization_link] using [ARB files][arb_documentation_link] for translations.
145: 
146: ### Adding Strings
147: 
148: 1. To add a new localizable string, open the `app_en.arb` file at `lib/l10n/arb/app_en.arb` and add a new key/value pair with the relevant description (optional):
149: 
150: ```arb
151: {
152:     "@@locale": "en",
153:     "counterAppBarTitle": "Counter",
154:     "@counterAppBarTitle": {
155:         "description": "Text shown in the AppBar of the Counter Page"
156:     },
157:     "helloWorld": "Hello World",
158:     "@helloWorld": {
159:         "description": "Hello World greeting."
160:     }
161: }
162: ```
163: 
164: 1. Use the new string:
165: 
166: ```dart
167: import 'package:temp_app/l10n/l10n.dart';
168: 
169: @override
170: Widget build(BuildContext context) {
171:   final l10n = context.l10n;
172:   return Text(l10n.helloWorld);
173: }
174: ```
175: 
176: ### Adding Supported Locales
177: 
178: Update the `CFBundleLocalizations` array in the `Info.plist` at `ios/Runner/Info.plist` to include the new locale.
179: 
180: ```xml
181:     ...
182: 
183:     <key>CFBundleLocalizations</key>
184: 	<array>
185: 		<string>en</string>
186: 		<string>es</string>
187: 	</array>
188: 
189:     ...
190: ```
191: 
192: ### Adding Translations
193: 
194: 1. For each supported locale, add a new ARB file in `lib/l10n/arb`:
195: 
196: ```
197: ├── l10n
198: │   ├── arb
199: │   │   ├── app_en.arb
200: │   │   └── app_es.arb
201: ```
202: 
203: 1. Add the translated strings to the new `.arb` file:
204: 
205: `app_es.arb`
206: 
207: ```arb
208: {
209:     "@@locale": "es",
210:     "counterAppBarTitle": "Contador",
211:     "@counterAppBarTitle": {
212:         "description": "Texto mostrado en la AppBar de la página del contador"
213:     },
214:     "helloWorld": "Hola Mundo",
215:     "@helloWorld": {
216:         "description": "Saludo Hola Mundo."
217:     }  
218: }
219: ```
220: 
221: ### Generating Translations
222: 
223: To use the latest translations changes, you will need to generate them:
224: 
225: ```sh
226: flutter gen-l10n --arb-dir="lib/l10n/arb"
227: ```
228: 
229: Alternatively, run `flutter run` and code generation will take place automatically.
